.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER.CONF 5 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-file-reaper.conf \- YAML configuration of the Mu2e DAQ file reaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration is a YAML mapping with the top-level keys
.BR reaper ", " database ", " discovery ", " api ", " defaults ", " areas " and " notifications .
Every scalar under
.BR reaper ", " database ", " discovery " and " api
may be overridden by an environment variable and by a command-line flag:
.PP
.RS
command line  >  environment (MU2EDAQ_FILE_REAPER_*)  >  .env  >  this file  >  defaults
.RE
.PP
Loading never aborts on a bad value: the problem is listed on the
.B /config
page and in
.BR "/api/v1/config" ,
the offending tier or area is dropped, and the rest applies.  Unknown keys are
reported.
.SH UNITS
.TP
Percentages
.BR 80 ", " "\[dq]80\[dq]" " or " "\[dq]80%\[dq]" .
Thresholds are percent of capacity
.B used
computed as
.IR "100 * used / (used + free)" ,
the
.BR df (1)
convention.
.TP
Durations
.BR "\[dq]90s\[dq] \[dq]10m\[dq] \[dq]6h\[dq] \[dq]7d\[dq] \[dq]2w\[dq]"
or bare seconds.
.TP
Sizes
SI (\[dq]500 GB\[dq]) or IEC (\[dq]500 GiB\[dq]) units, or bare bytes
(reserved for future use; the reaper's thresholds are percentages).
.SH THE reaper SECTION
.TP
.B label
Instance label (default: short hostname).  Appears in discovery, notification
titles and the UI.
.TP
.BR web_host " (0.0.0.0), " web_port " (5004)"
Web UI and API listener.
.TP
.B api_port
Optional second listener serving only
.BR /api/* .
.TP
.B scan_interval
Seconds between scans (default 600).
.TP
.B dry_run
When true nothing is modified; queues, history and notifications behave as in
a live run and disk usage is simulated from the planned actions.
.TP
.BR daemon ", " pid_file ", " log_file ", " log_max_bytes " (10485760), " log_backup_count " (5)"
Process and logging.  The start script always passes
.BR \-\-daemon .
.TP
.B admin_token
Secret unlocking the mutating pages of the UI and the
.B X-Admin-Token
header of the API.  Empty: a one-time bootstrap token is logged at startup.
Put it in the environment or the .env file rather than here.
.TP
.B workers
Concurrent area scans (default 4).  Areas on one filesystem never act at the
same time regardless.
.TP
.B max_passes_per_scan
Passes per scan (default 3).  Each pass re-measures and re-enumerates; the
most severe active tier acts first and lower tiers follow when it stops.
.TP
.B remeasure_every
Re-read disk usage after every N actions (default 1).
.TP
.B stall_window
Actions between checks that used space really dropped (default 20).  When
less than a quarter of the expected drop is observed the pass stops with a
.B space_not_reclaimed
alarm (files are probably held open elsewhere).
.TP
.B shutdown_grace_s
Seconds to wait for in-flight actions on SIGTERM (default 30).
.TP
.B queue_publish_limit
Queue entries exposed per area in the UI and API (default 1000).
.TP
.B history_log_queue_adds
.BR all ", " new_only " (default) or " none :
how many
.B queue_add
history rows a scan writes.
.TP
.B compress_verify
.BR crc " (default), " size " or " none :
verification of every compressed file before the original is removed.
.TP
.B compress_min_ratio
Skip (and remember) files whose compressed size is not below this fraction of
the original (default 0.95).
.TP
.B compress_assumed_ratio
Compressed/original ratio assumed in dry runs (default 0.5).
.TP
.B protected_paths
Absolute paths that must never be touched, in addition to the FTS database
and the reaper's own database.
.TP
.B allow_shallow_root
Allow an area directly under
.I /
such as
.IR /scratch .
System directories are refused regardless.
.TP
.B fake_usage_file
Test hook: a JSON file mapping an area realpath to
.IR "[total, used, free]" ,
re-read on every measurement.  Never set in production; the daemon warns
whenever it is active.
.SH THE database SECTION
.TP
.B url
SQLAlchemy URL.  Default
.IR sqlite:///./data/file-reaper.db
(WAL mode, busy timeout 5 s).  PostgreSQL:
.IR postgresql+psycopg://user:password@host/dbname
with the
.B psycopg
package installed.
.TP
.B history_retention_days
History and notification-log rows older than this are pruned once a day
(default 365; 0 keeps everything).
.SH THE discovery SECTION
.TP
.BR enabled " (true), " app " (file-reaper), " name " (default \[dq]File Reaper (<label>)\[dq])"
mu2edaq-discovery record.  The label, API port and area count are published
in
.IR meta .
.SH THE api SECTION
.TP
.B open_read
When true (default) GET endpoints need no token.  Mutating endpoints always
need a bearer token or an admin session.
.SH THE defaults AND areas SECTIONS
Every key below may appear under
.B defaults
(inherited by every area) and under an individual area (overriding the
default).
.TP
.B path
Area directory (areas only, required).  Local paths only.
.TP
.B name
Identifier used in URLs, the API and the CLI (default: the path with slashes
replaced by dashes, e.g.
.IR data-raw ).
.TP
.B label
Human name shown in the UI.
.TP
.B enabled
false configures the area but never scans it until an operator enables it.
.TP
.B thresholds
Mapping of
.BR warning ", " critical ", " full
to percent used (defaults 80, 90, 95).
.TP
.B tiers
Mapping of tier name to a block with:
.RS
.TP
.B policy
.BR LRU-Delete ", " Age-Delete ", " LRU-Compress " or " Age-Compress
(defaults: warning LRU-Compress, critical LRU-Delete, full Age-Delete).
.TP
.B min_age
Minimum age on the policy's ordering key (defaults 7d, 3d, 1d).
.TP
.BR low_water " (10), " high_water " (0)"
Percent below and above the threshold giving the stop and trigger points:
trigger = min(threshold + high_water, 100), stop = max(threshold \- low_water, 0).
.TP
.B threshold
Overrides the value from
.BR thresholds .
.TP
.B compressor
Overrides the area's algorithm for this tier.
.RE
.IP
Setting a tier to
.B null
disables it.  An area with no tiers is monitor-only.
.TP
.BR include " ([\[dq]*\[dq]]), " exclude
Globs matched against the area-relative path and the basename.  The default
exclude list covers temporary and database files.  Exclude wins.
.TP
.B settle_seconds
Files modified more recently than this are never touched (default 300).
.TP
.B fts_db
Path to a mu2edaq-fts SQLite database.  When set, only files whose FTS status
is COMPLETED or DELETED (or the reaper-compressed copy of such a file) are
eligible.  An unreadable database makes nothing eligible and raises an alarm.
.TP
.B compression
Block with
.BR algorithm " (gzip, bz2, xz, zstd), " level " (6) and " skip_suffixes
(files already carrying one of these suffixes are never compressed).
.TP
.B prune_empty_dirs
Remove directories left empty by deletions, never the area root (default
false).
.TP
.B max_actions_per_scan
Hard cap per scan (0 = unlimited).
.TP
.B check_open_files
Reject files another process has open, using a
.I /proc
scan (Linux; expensive; default false).
.TP
.B allow_hardlinks
Act on files with more than one link (default false; deleting one link frees
nothing).
.SH THE notifications SECTION
.TP
.B rate_limit_seconds
Identical (channel, area, title) events are suppressed within this window
unless the severity increased (default 600).  A failed send is retried on the
next event.
.TP
.B max_per_hour
Cap on sends per rolling hour (0 = unlimited).
.PP
Each channel has
.BR enabled " and " min_severity
(debug < info < warning < error < critical).  Tier activation maps
warning to warning, critical to error and full to critical; a policy that
cannot clear its tier is error (critical for the full tier); recoveries are
info.
.TP
.B mu2e_notify
.BR source ", " category ", " url ", " token .
The phone notification server is found via discovery when
.B url
is null.  Needs the
.B mu2edaq-notify
package.
.TP
.B daq_messages
.BR host ", " port " (5555), " subsystem ", " event_category .
ZMQ PUSH to the DAQ message dashboard; needs
.BR pyzmq .
.TP
.B bigredbox
.BR port " (37020), " system_id ", " ip .
UDP broadcast to the control-room Big Red Box; default min_severity critical.
.TP
.B email
.BR method " (smtp | mail), " smtp_host ", " smtp_port ", " starttls ", " username ", " password ", " from ", " to .
.TP
.B slack
.BR webhook_url .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
reaper:
  label: dl-01
  web_port: 5004
  scan_interval: 600
  dry_run: true
database:
  url: "sqlite:///./data/file-reaper-dl-01.db"
defaults:
  settle_seconds: 600
areas:
  - path: /data/raw
    label: "Raw data"
    fts_db: /home/mu2edaq/mu2edaq-main/mu2edaq-fts/fts_status.db
    thresholds: {warning: 75, critical: 85, full: 92}
    tiers:
      warning:  {policy: LRU-Compress, min_age: "14d"}
      critical: {policy: LRU-Delete,   min_age: "7d"}
      full:     {policy: Age-Delete,   min_age: "2d", low_water: 12}
  - path: /daqlogs
    include: ["*.log", "*.log.*"]
    tiers:
      warning:  {policy: Age-Compress, min_age: "2d"}
      critical: {policy: Age-Delete,   min_age: "30d"}
      full:     {policy: Age-Delete,   min_age: "7d", low_water: 15}
    prune_empty_dirs: true
notifications:
  mu2e_notify:  {enabled: true, min_severity: warning, source: file-reaper, category: DAQ}
  daq_messages: {enabled: true, min_severity: warning, host: mu2e-mgr-01.fnal.gov, port: 5555}
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml
Reference configuration with every key commented.
.TP
.I config/.env.example
Secrets template (
.BR MU2EDAQ_FILE_REAPER_ADMIN_TOKEN ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1),
.BR mu2edaq-reaper (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-api (7)
